Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["GWPNumerical Extension Package", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001159200180174*^9, 
  4.001159236404915*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"abee1d4b-5339-49e2-b2c6-\
02a4738e187e"],

Cell["Jeremy B. Maddox", "Author",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988201532003448*^9, 
  3.988201536787407*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ce5db93c-ecf9-4e20-ba23-\
5eebb8abef95"],

Cell["\<\
Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry
Western Kentucky University
Bowling Green, KY 42101-1079
Email: jeremy.maddox@wku.edu\
\>", "Affiliation",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988201549259402*^9, 
  3.988201579115401*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1c460c36-6277-461e-857c-\
8aa5d6b29b90"],

Cell["\<\
The GWPNumerical extension generalizes the GWPTools Mathematica package to \
arbitrary time-dependent quadratic potentials and non-stationary thermal \
environments across all pure-state (1D, 2D, SS1D, MC1D) and open-system \
(RDM1D) wavepacket engines. By exploiting the exact Gaussian structure of the \
wavepacket and reduced density matrix ansatzes, GWPNumerical replaces \
expensive spatiotemporal grid propagation with compact sets of ordinary \
differential equations (ODEs) solved via cached NDSolveValue routines. \
Unitary propagators directly integrate the coupled Riccati shape and \
continuous phase equations (automatically tracking unwrapped Maslov phases \
across caustics), while the open-system Caldeira\[Dash]Leggett propagator \
utilizes a three-stage linear phase-space covariance pipeline that remains \
unconditionally stable across stiff mechanical and thermal ramps. Fully \
compatible with all existing GWPTools property queries and visualization \
tools, GWPNumerical provides both a high-precision benchmarking standard for \
quantum trajectory methods and a fast, interactive calculator for modeling \
pulsed laser control, multidimensional mode-mixing, and nonequilibrium \
quantum thermodynamics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.001679116126563*^9, {4.001679424099743*^9, 
   4.001679424729988*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fc200574-4456-46bd-835d-\
5c070627338e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Loading the Package", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001199820045351*^9, 4.001199824804768*^9}, {
  4.001494548143758*^9, 4.00149455235131*^9}, {4.0015021267044983`*^9, 
  4.001502142182994*^9}, {4.001689878364676*^9, 
  4.001689893247569*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"11e7d904-162f-4b22-94b9-\
a01c4b0a2166"],

Cell["\<\
Rather than forcing every session to load all multidimensional, \
multi-component, and open-system numerical solvers at startup, the master \
orchestrator package GWPNumerical dynamically inspects which core GWPTools \
engines are currently active in the Wolfram session and selectively loads the \
corresponding numerical extensions, registering their \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Numerical\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NumericalCL\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) potential \
templates into GWPRegistry.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0011998285310297`*^9, 4.001199834424795*^9}, 
   4.001494319285102*^9, {4.0014944843389053`*^9, 
   4.0014944937792263`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d215bc8c-0d43-42de-8896-\
d207e6a06d80"],

Cell["\<\
Because GWPNumerical checks the active context path at the moment it is \
called, any optional engines (2D, SS1D, MC1D, or RDM1D) should be loaded \
prior to calling GWPNumerical (note that GWPEngine1D is loaded automatically \
by the base GWPTools package).

Here is an example of initializing the complete suite of engines alongside \
the numerical extension:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.001494349795733*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b68752ba-4033-40ee-8e6e-\
4f766a4706f4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Quit", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0021802888274117`*^9, 4.002180290676784*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[93]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ff31b89b-9e8f-4265-b3bc-b6702fd37dfb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/jrm82302/maddox/Projects/Mathematica/GWPTools\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<MaddoxScience`GWPTools`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<MaddoxScience`GWPTools`GWPEngine2D`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<MaddoxScience`GWPTools`GWPEngineSS1D`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<MaddoxScience`GWPTools`GWPEngineMC1D`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<MaddoxScience`GWPTools`GWPEngineRDM1D`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<MaddoxScience`GWPTools`GWPNumerical`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0014945162549267`*^9, 4.001494533535928*^9}, {
  4.001494640767058*^9, 4.00149464197995*^9}, {4.0016674313352633`*^9, 
  4.00166744865396*^9}, {4.001667489291391*^9, 4.00166749363282*^9}, {
  4.001683244728006*^9, 4.001683314846572*^9}, {4.0016890471384172`*^9, 
  4.0016890515687513`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f1751ed4-52c1-48eb-b593-606a2d0ff934"],

Cell["\<\
As detailed in the next section, GWPNumerical automatically caches the \
InterpolatingFunction solutions generated by NDSolveValue to accelerate \
repeated property queries. However, because this cache is indexed by the \
symbols passed into the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Potential\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] option, modifying a parameter inside a named \
potential function (such as changing a ramp rate or coupling constant within \
v2Ramp[t_]) will not automatically trigger a fresh integration if the \
function symbol itself remains unchanged.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.00170269401171*^9, 4.001702701027337*^9}, {
  4.001702740009365*^9, 4.001702775696542*^9}, {4.0017029128746023`*^9, 
  4.0017029163205137`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"81e82046-8584-4f2d-87b1-\
8975e7cf01ef"],

Cell["\<\
Calling GWPClearCache[] strips all stored numerical trajectories from memory \
while preserving the underlying solver definitions, forcing NDSolveValue to \
re-integrate the equations of motion on the next query.  Use as needed if you \
wish to modify the Example Problems (below) that use parameterized functions.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001702930001392*^9, 4.001702994872335*^9}, {
  4.0017042407297287`*^9, 
  4.001704258749206*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ba99131d-48be-4b4e-9545-\
77b43b2ba3c0"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Software Architecture", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001199753595174*^9, 4.001199797614334*^9}, 
   4.001494087245859*^9},ExpressionUUID->"7d2ecf24-2e21-4971-94ab-\
2d3ff368d66f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Function Slot Paradigm", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001492437440769*^9, 4.001492442388365*^9}, 
   4.0015030231813107`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"0f121fed-eda0-4453-9f64-\
ca7d6624952a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "GWPNumerical provides two new potential models.  \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Numerical\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is used to calculate \
the unitary evolution for a given wavepacket type.  \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NumericalCL\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is an additional \
model specifically for the RDM1D engine (reduced density matrix) and is used \
to calculate dissipative dynamics according to the Caldeira-Leggett master \
equation, which features a friction parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "d"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "db312771-51b1-4bd1-b29c-cd4d55b801c3"],
 " and thermal energy  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["k", "B"], "T"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dfb8fae-8621-425a-8c1e-f4b6c68bcbd2"],
 " associated with a thermal bath."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001456468009556*^9, 4.001456748944971*^9}, {
   4.001456827138156*^9, 4.001456863054326*^9}, {4.001489057113583*^9, 
   4.001489089571373*^9}, {4.00149238962595*^9, 4.0014923962180862`*^9}, 
   4.001683551959093*^9},ExpressionUUID->"8bac3fb7-2b86-4ff5-9f3c-\
fcc526f1c3ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["IMPORTANT",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": In all \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Numerical\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]NumericalCL\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] potential \
specifications, the quadratic potential coefficients and bath parameters are \
evaluated inside NDSolveValue as v0[t], v1[t], v2[t], gamma[t], and kT[t].  \
Therefore, every potential and bath argument passed to a numerical model must \
be a callable function of a single time argument (either a pure function \
using # and &, or the symbol name of a defined function)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.00115947397963*^9, {4.001456794444456*^9, 4.001456797447748*^9}, {
   4.001489114017417*^9, 4.001489186847196*^9}, {4.001501876510285*^9, 
   4.001501877067972*^9}, 
   4.001705081054316*^9},ExpressionUUID->"00dd16aa-0258-42d4-af51-\
56ddfcad6313"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Example 1: Using pure functions (with # and &)", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001501938853764*^9, 
  4.001501961212688*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"589016c7-1f0f-428e-a863-\
4d63763fd29f"],

Cell["\<\
This example shows the correct usage of pure functions where the potential \
coefficients are just simply constant values.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016836541630774`*^9, 
  4.001683700304653*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"370fbb7c-37a3-4018-94a6-\
7cfea88a1d20"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"m", "=", "1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"omega", "=", "1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tMin", "=", "0"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tMax", "=", 
   RowBox[{"3", "*", "2", "*", "Pi"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"obj", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GWP", "[", "\"\<1D\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Potential\>\"", "->", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Numerical\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], " ", "*", " ", "m", " ", "*", " ", 
         RowBox[{"omega", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "tMin", ",", 
      "tMax"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Code",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{
